Architectural Philosophy
Traditional AI models rely on stochastic inference (probabilistic next-token prediction). This approach necessitates heavy driver-level interrupts and constant OS context-switching, leading to significant latency accumulation.

SAIHV utilizes a Deterministic Hardware-Reflex Arc. By interfacing directly with memory-mapped silicon logic, we bypass the software-interrupt stack entirely, eliminating traditional synchronization overhead.

Key Advantages
Constant-Time Scaling: Performance remains deterministic regardless of node count or signal load.

Silicon-Native Reflex: Bypasses the "Inference Trap" by resolving logic at the hardware boundary.

Anti-Fragile Concurrency: Maintains stability under conditions that typically cause jitter in standard inference clusters.

